# ANV-0038 -- the lease margin was one clock bound where it needed two
# the declared bound is how far ONE node's clock may be from true time; a
# handover involves two, and they can be wrong in opposite directions
seed        = 3
workload    = shard_kv
nodes       = 5
faults      = drawn from seed; needs clock offsets pointing apart
invariant   = INV-SHARD-04 (at most one valid lease per range at any instant)
reproduce   = anvil_shard_faults 12
note        = also on seeds 4, 8 and 10. The clock model was inside the bound it
              declared on all of them, so this was the implementation being
              wrong rather than the environment.
found_at    = P5
fixed_at    = P5
